# name: test/sql/tabfm_download_runtime.test
# description: tabfm_download_runtime's declaration surface — the parts that
#              need no network. The cuda wheel flow and (once a release
#              carries plugins) the plugin fetch are exercised on real
#              hardware via tools/gpu_test/; what CI can pin is that the
#              error paths name their fixes and never a URL that does not
#              exist (docs/GPU_HARDENING_PLAN.md P7).
# group: [anofox_tabfm]

require anofox_tabfm

statement ok
LOAD anofox_tabfm

# A plugin-carrying release is pinned (v2026.08.22), so 'rocm' now performs a
# real fetch — which CI must not depend on. The fetch itself is exercised by
# the hardware harness (tools/gpu_test) and the post-release end-to-end;
# what stays pinned here is the network-free declaration surface below.

# An unknown backend is refused with the accepted set.
statement error
CALL tabfm_download_runtime('tpu')
----
<REGEX>:.*unknown backend 'tpu'.*expected 'cuda' or 'rocm'.*
